{"chunk_id": "332682be7cc7", "text": "Rama and Ravana continue their colossal duel, battling across sky, ground, and mountain while gods, demons, and spirits watch. For seven days neither warrior yields. Seeing no clear victory, Matali\u2014the charioteer of the gods\u2014reminds Rama of his true power and urges him to use Brahma\u2019s divine weapon, whose use has been foretold by the gods. Rama prepares the celestial arrow given by the sage Agastya, a cosmic missile embodying wind, fire, sun, and the elements. After invoking sacred formulas, he releases it with immense force. The irresistible shaft pierces Ravana\u2019s chest, extinguishing his life before returning to Rama\u2019s quiver. Ravana falls like the demon Vritra struck by Indra\u2019s thunderbolt. With their king dead, the rakshasas flee toward Lanka while the victorious monkey army pursues them, marking the decisive end of the war\u2019s central tyrant.\nAfter a long battle, Rama uses Brahma\u2019s divine weapon to strike Ravana in the chest, killing him and routing the remaining Rakshasas.\nThemes: final battle, divine weapons, fate and prophecy, death of Ravana, triumph of Rama", "vector": [-0.007450613658875227, -0.02253810688853264, -0.020475883036851883, -0.0008614772232249379, -0.005202124826610088, 0.010929783806204796, -0.032942354679107666, -0.01652439683675766, -0.028099456802010536, -0.021393904462456703, 0.007982800714671612, 0.01589907705783844, 0.006758770905435085, 0.00786305870860815, -0.0009562729392200708, 0.019544556736946106, 0.03158527985215187, -0.012193727307021618, 0.025691311806440353, -0.007517137099057436, 0.005099013913422823, -0.0077965352684259415, -0.007357480935752392, 0.02007674239575863, -0.017296068370342255, -0.0004373909323476255, 0.023855268955230713, -0.03211746737360954, 0.01623169332742691, -0.02232523262500763, -0.0007217781967483461, -0.0075503988191485405, -0.002793980063870549, 0.0021586823277175426, -0.011461971327662468, 0.004067901987582445, 0.00554472021